.TH SPRITEPLOT3D 1
.SH NAME
spriteplot3d \- a mesh sprite turning under a matrix
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/spriteplot3d
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I SpritePlot3D
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/SpritePlot3D.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
A mesh sprite rotates about X once every hundred frames and about Z once
every hundred and thirty.  The two rates share no common factor, so the
model never repeats an attitude.  It is drawn without perspective against
a depth buffer.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B "any key"
Exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/spriteplot3d.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR spriteedit (1),
.IR wm (1)
